message: "If you use the negative-results ledger, the research methodology, or the findings from this project, please cite it as below."
title: "Aegis Finance: an open, self-auditing quantitative research pipeline with pre-registered trials and published negative results"
authors:
  - family-names: "Abdullaev"
    given-names: "Murathan"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Murathanx12/Aegis-Finance"
url: "https://aegis-finance-six.vercel.app"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-06-08"
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - backtest overfitting
  - pre-registration
  - negative results
  - multiple testing
  - deflated Sharpe ratio
  - point-in-time data
abstract: >-
  A free, open-source market-intelligence platform whose distinguishing feature
  is research discipline: 179 strategy candidates screened under an
  explore/confirm wall with placebo gates, 31 documented negative results, a
  live forward paper track record (inception 2026-06-08) with tamper-evident
  configuration hashes, and a policy of no skill claims before 24 months of
  forward record. Includes reusable findings on data leakage, fabricated
  quantile spreads, placebo-gate miscalibration, and multiple-testing
  arithmetic at retail scale.
